#N canvas 0 50 1040 1390 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   mellotron~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 mellotron style tape keyboard for your own wav files;
#X text 30 86 a keyboard of tapes. load your own wav files onto the keys and each key plays its tape from the start. the tape stops after a few seconds like the real machine until you release the key. wow flutter drift hiss and tone loss. a built-in synthetic stand-in plays when no samples are loaded. sixteen voices., f 110;
#X text 30 166 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 210 each voice reads a tape (a wav file) with linear interpolation at a rate that follows the key. wow flutter and drift are slow modulations of that rate., f 110;
#X text 30 260 the tape clock runs while the key is down. when it reaches the tape length the sound stops (or loops if loop is on)., f 110;
#X text 30 310 without samples a voice synthesizes a flute strings or choir stand-in. no samples are shipped with this object., f 110;
#X text 30 370 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 414 1  open the engine page below and turn dsp on, f 110;
#X text 30 444 2  play a midi keyboard or click chord on, f 110;
#X text 30 474 3  open the parameters page and move any control or open presets and step through the sounds, f 110;
#X text 30 504 4  everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy, f 110;
#X text 30 564 try:  send samples tapes with a folder of wav files named 48.wav 50.wav 52.wav and so on (the number is the midi note), f 110;
#X text 30 614 try:  raise wow and drift for a seasick tape or turn them down for a clean one, f 110;
#X text 30 644 try:  turn loop on and set length short for a tape that cycles forever, f 110;
#X text 30 688 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 732 no sound: turn dsp on in the engine page and check the volume slider. the synth needs a note: click chord on or play a midi key, f 110;
#X text 30 782 nothing changes after a rebuild: pd keeps the old external in memory so close every patch and restart pd, f 110;
#X text 30 812 a note is stuck: send panic. a missing note off from a midi device is the usual cause, f 110;
#X text 30 842 unknown parameter in the console: names are exact and lowercase so send params to print them all, f 110;
#X text 30 872 a bank file is not found: save and load names are relative to the folder of this patch, f 110;
#X text 30 902 the sliders do not move when you change a preset: the object must be created with the same name as in the boxes. default name is the object name, f 110;
#X text 30 952 clicks or dropouts: raise the audio buffer in the pd audio settings or lower the voice count in the creation argument, f 110;
#X text 30 1002 samples says failed: the folder must contain .wav files (8 16 24 or 32-bit) and the path is relative to this patch, f 110;
#X text 30 1052 the sound stops after eight seconds: that is the tape. raise length or turn loop on, f 110;
#X text 30 1082 wrong pitch: name each file with its root midi note like 48.wav. a single file without a number is treated as middle c, f 110;
#X text 30 1146 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 940 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 presets: factory sounds are stored as plain text and every control above is a message. click a box to load that sound, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; mellotron preset 0;
#X text 250 112 0  flute tape;
#X msg 30 144 \; mellotron preset 1;
#X text 250 146 1  string tape;
#X msg 30 178 \; mellotron preset 2;
#X text 250 180 2  choir tape;
#X msg 30 212 \; mellotron preset 3;
#X text 250 214 3  worn tape;
#X msg 460 110 \; mellotron preset 4;
#X text 680 112 4  clean tape;
#X msg 460 144 \; mellotron preset 5;
#X text 680 146 5  short tape;
#X msg 460 178 \; mellotron preset 6;
#X text 680 180 6  looping pad;
#X msg 460 212 \; mellotron preset 7;
#X text 680 214 7  seasick choir;
#X text 30 266 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 310 20 0 0 0 - mellotron-name - 0;
#X floatatom 230 310 4 0 0 0 - mellotron-index - 0;
#X text 340 312 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 354 \; mellotron next;
#X msg 198 354 \; mellotron prev;
#X msg 366 354 \; mellotron mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 394 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1, f 100;
#X text 30 444 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 488 \; mellotron A;
#X msg 174 488 \; mellotron B;
#X text 318 490 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 530 morph;
#X obj 110 528 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-morph mellotron-morph-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 572 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every parameter blends smoothly between the two, f 100;
#X text 30 622 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 666 \; mellotron store mysound;
#X msg 270 666 \; mellotron save my.bank;
#X msg 502 666 \; mellotron load my.bank;
#X text 30 706 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load adds the sounds from a text file, f 100;
#X text 30 756 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 800 every slider in the parameters page sends to mellotron-name and listens on mellotron-name-r so the stash library can store and morph whole scenes: create [stash/bank mellotron] and send it a scan message for a saved copy of the parameters page. this follows the stash naming rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 1190 pd presets;
#X text 30 1224 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1500 1064 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every control here is also a message: set name value with values from 0 to 1. switches take the step number shown under each one, f 120;
#X text 30 66 --- tape ---;
#X text 30 106 tape sound  -  set tape;
#X obj 30 138 hradio 18 1 0 3 mellotron-tape mellotron-tape-r empty 0 -8 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0;
#X text 30 170 0..2 : flute | strings | choir (stand-in when no wav files are loaded), f 34;
#X text 30 244 tape length  -  set length;
#X obj 30 276 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-length mellotron-length-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 382 loop tape  -  set loop;
#X obj 30 414 hradio 18 1 0 2 mellotron-loop mellotron-loop-r empty 0 -8 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0;
#X text 30 446 0..1 : off | on, f 34;
#X text 30 520 pitch control  -  set pitch;
#X obj 30 552 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-pitch mellotron-pitch-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 350 66 --- tape character ---;
#X text 350 106 wow  -  set wow;
#X obj 350 138 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-wow mellotron-wow-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 350 244 flutter  -  set flutter;
#X obj 350 276 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-flutter mellotron-flutter-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 350 382 drift  -  set drift;
#X obj 350 414 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-drift mellotron-drift-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 650 106 tone  -  set tone;
#X obj 650 138 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-tone mellotron-tone-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 650 244 tape hiss  -  set hiss;
#X obj 650 276 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-hiss mellotron-hiss-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 970 66 --- envelope ---;
#X text 970 106 attack  -  set att;
#X obj 970 138 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-att mellotron-att-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 970 244 release  -  set rel;
#X obj 970 276 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-rel mellotron-rel-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 688 --- output ---;
#X text 30 728 velocity  -  set vel;
#X obj 30 760 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-vel mellotron-vel-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 866 volume  -  set vol;
#X obj 30 898 hsl 190 18 0 1 0 0 mellotron-vol mellotron-vol-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X restore 220 1190 pd parameters;
#X text 220 1224 every control, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1158 messages 0;
#X text 30 16 click any box to send it to the synth. the synth receives everything through its name so you can use [s mellotron] from anywhere in your patch, f 110;
#X msg 30 66 \; mellotron note 60 100;
#X text 334 68 play midi note 60 at velocity 100 (velocity 0 is note off);
#X msg 30 100 \; mellotron note 60 0;
#X text 334 102 release note 60;
#X msg 30 134 \; mellotron bend 0.5;
#X text 334 136 pitch bend from -1 to 1 (size set by bendrange);
#X msg 30 168 \; mellotron bendrange 12;
#X text 334 170 bend range in semitones (default 2);
#X msg 30 202 \; mellotron mod 0.5;
#X text 334 204 mod wheel from 0 to 1 (more lfo);
#X msg 30 236 \; mellotron aftertouch 0.5;
#X text 334 238 channel pressure from 0 to 1 (opens the filter);
#X msg 30 270 \; mellotron sustain 1;
#X text 334 272 sustain pedal (1 down and 0 up);
#X msg 30 304 \; mellotron panic;
#X text 334 306 silence everything immediately;
#X msg 30 338 \; mellotron set tone 0.3;
#X text 334 340 set one parameter by name (see the parameters page);
#X msg 30 372 \; mellotron params;
#X text 334 374 print every parameter name to the pd window;
#X msg 30 406 \; mellotron preset 3;
#X text 334 408 load preset number 3 (counting from 0);
#X msg 30 440 \; mellotron next;
#X text 334 442 next preset (wraps around);
#X msg 30 474 \; mellotron prev;
#X text 334 476 previous preset;
#X msg 30 508 \; mellotron mutate 0.3;
#X text 334 510 random variation of the current sound from 0 to 1;
#X msg 30 542 \; mellotron A;
#X text 334 544 remember the current sound as a;
#X msg 30 576 \; mellotron B;
#X text 334 578 remember the current sound as b;
#X msg 30 610 \; mellotron morph 0.5;
#X text 334 612 blend between a and b;
#X msg 30 644 \; mellotron store mysound;
#X text 334 646 keep the current sound in the user bank after the factory presets;
#X msg 30 678 \; mellotron save my.bank;
#X text 334 680 write the user bank to a text file next to this patch;
#X msg 30 712 \; mellotron load my.bank;
#X text 334 714 add the presets from a text file to the user bank;
#X msg 30 746 \; mellotron data 0.5;
#X text 334 748 data inlet: any number from 0 to 1 (a sensor or a csv column) that drives mapped parameters;
#X msg 30 780 \; mellotron datamap tone 0.3;
#X text 334 782 map data to a parameter: it moves up to 0.3 either side (a negative amount inverts);
#X msg 30 814 \; mellotron datamap clear;
#X text 334 816 remove all data mappings (up to four at once);
#X msg 30 848 \; mellotron samples tapes;
#X text 334 850 load every wav in the folder tapes next to this patch (name each file with its midi note like 48.wav);
#X msg 30 882 \; mellotron sample 60 c4.wav;
#X text 334 884 put one wav on the key for midi note 60;
#X msg 30 916 \; mellotron samples clear;
#X text 334 918 unload all tapes and go back to the synthetic stand-in;
#X text 30 964 --- outlets of the object ---;
#X text 30 1008 outlet 1 audio left   outlet 2 audio right   outlet 3 preset name as a symbol   outlet 4 list with preset index and preset count, f 110;
#X text 30 1058 create it as [mellotron~]  or  [mellotron~ name]  or  [mellotron~ name 8]   where name is the prefix used by every box and 8 is the voice count, f 110;
#X restore 410 1190 pd messages;
#X text 410 1224 clickable list, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1300 examples 0;
#X text 30 16 copy these into your own patch. they all talk to [mellotron~] through [s mellotron] so the engine page must be running with dsp on, f 130;
